abstract: >-
  A practical Quality Engineering and security framework for testing MCP-powered
  AI agents across protocol conformance, tool and resource contracts,
  authentication, authorization, business rules, agent tool selection,
  arguments, trajectories, human approval, prompt injection, tool poisoning,
  tenant isolation, reliability, observability, performance and CI/CD release
  gates. The work emphasizes that discovery is not permission, MCP must not
  bypass authoritative application authorization, and agent quality must be
  proven from execution evidence rather than final-response plausibility.
